      <Body>
         <P1group>
            <Title>Citation and extent</Title>
            <P1 id="article-1">
               <Pnumber>1</Pnumber>
               <P1para>
                  <P2 id="article-1-1">
                     <Pnumber>1</Pnumber>
                     <P2para>
                        <Text>This Order may be cited as the Coroners and Justice Act 2009 (Commencement No. 21) Order 2023.</Text>
                     </P2para>
                  </P2>
                  <P2 id="article-1-2">
                     <Pnumber>2</Pnumber>
                     <P2para>
                        <Text>This Order extends to England and Wales.</Text>
                     </P2para>
                  </P2>
               </P1para>
            </P1>
         </P1group>
         <P1group>
            <Title>Commencement of provisions of the Coroners and Justice Act 2009</Title>
            <P1 id="article-2">
               <Pnumber>2</Pnumber>
               <P1para>
                  <Text>The following provisions of the Coroners and Justice Act 2009 come into force on 1st October 2023—</Text>
                  <P3 id="article-2-a">
                     <Pnumber>a</Pnumber>
                     <P3para>
                        <Text>section 19 (medical examiners: supplementary)<FootnoteRef Ref="f00002"/>, and</Text>
                     </P3para>
                  </P3>
                  <P3 id="article-2-b">
                     <Pnumber>b</Pnumber>
                     <P3para>
                        <Text>section 20 (medical certificate of cause of death)<FootnoteRef Ref="f00003"/>.</Text>
                     </P3para>
                  </P3>
               </P1para>
            </P1>
         </P1group>
         <SignedSection>
            <Signatory>
               <Signee>
                  <PersonName>Markham</PersonName>
                  <JobTitle>Parliamentary Under Secretary of State</JobTitle>
                  <DateSigned Date="2023-09-20">
                     <DateText>20th September 2023</DateText>
                  </DateSigned>
                  <Department>Department of Health and Social Care</Department>
               </Signee>
            </Signatory>
         </SignedSection>
      </Body>
      <ExplanatoryNotes>
         <Title>Explanatory Note</Title>
         <Comment>
            <Para>
               <Text>(This note is not part of the Order)</Text>
            </Para>
         </Comment>
         <P>
            <Text>This Order commences sections 19 and 20 of the Coroners and Justice Act 2009 (c. 25) on 1st October 2023.</Text>
         </P>
         <P>
            <Text>Section 19 makes provision in relation to the appointment of medical examiners and confers powers on appropriate Ministers to make regulations in relation to medical examiners.</Text>
         </P>
         <P>
            <Text>Section 20 confers a power on the Secretary of State to make regulations in relation to the preparation of medical certificates of cause of death.</Text>
         </P>
      </ExplanatoryNotes>
